# SABOTAGE: ADR-048 §8 P13's MANDATORY anti-tautology positive control 2 (T218 / batch C2,
# §10 row 4 RATIFIED (a)), restated for issue #72 (ruled option 1) — the fold's input
# bill is a CONSTANT of at most 1 token instead of what its summarize call REPORTED
# spending, so a summarize that read a large span bills as if it read almost nothing.
# Before #72 the bill was `est_tokens/1` of the folded bytes and this patch pinned that;
# #72 made the bill the provider's own usage and the patch pins THAT now.
#
# Flips P13 POSITIVE CONTROL 2: the run's input total no longer equals the ordinary turns'
# 300 plus the fold ledger's own recorded input (which records the reported usage), and the
# bill no longer equals the summarize call's reported usage. The bare `> 300` inequality
# would NOT catch it (300 + 1 > 300); only the ledger-pinned equalities do.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/ai/agent_compaction_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: P13 POSITIVE CONTROL 2 (anti-tautology, MANDATORY): the fold DID spend real tokens against max_input_tokens/max_output_tokens in the same window
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/agent.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/agent.ex
index bb202cc..b52a285 100644
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/agent.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/agent.ex
@@ -1550,7 +1550,9 @@ defmodule Samen.AI.Agent do
   defp bill_summarizer!(%Run{} = run, %{input_tokens: in_tokens, output_tokens: out_tokens}) do
     run
     |> Ash.Changeset.for_update(:advance, %{
-      input_tokens_used: run.input_tokens_used + in_tokens,
+      # SABOTAGE (ADR-048 §8 P13 CONTROL 2; issue #72): the fold bills a CONSTANT of at
+      # most 1 input token instead of what its summarize call reported spending.
+      input_tokens_used: run.input_tokens_used + min(in_tokens, 1),
       output_tokens_used: run.output_tokens_used + out_tokens
     })
     |> Ash.update!(authorize?: false)
